{{box title="Status of this page"}}
Draft. Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims traceable to the Foundation.

* No primary data: no resident, relative or care worker observed or interviewed.
* References cited from memory; checked in the evidence pass (Open item O-1).
* Cells marked [threshold - O-2] still need numbers.
{{/box}}

**Abstract.** Eight objectives, three use cases, six functions. UC01: a walk with a fellow resident, the main use case. UC02: a walk on the phone with a relative. UC03: a walk on your own. Six Premises verify that the Functions work; ten Claims, five of them adverse, test whether they help.

= Objectives =

== Objective - Talk recovers [OBJ-01] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-01
|Name|Talk recovers
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-04; PS-01, PS-02. HFC-03, HFC-05.
|Statement|After a slip, the conversation goes on, without the slip being exposed.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|Goal on SA-04; HFC-03 Conversation repair
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Walk with company [OBJ-02] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-02
|Name|Walk with company
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goals on SA-01 to SA-03. HFC-01. Forbes et al. (2015).
|Statement|Residents walk more often with a fellow resident, a relative on the phone, or the guide where agreed.
|Type|Operational
|Derived from|Goals on SA-01 to SA-03; HV-06
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Safe while talking [OBJ-03] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-03
|Name|Safe while talking
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|VT-01; HFC-02. Lundin-Olsson et al. (1997).
|Statement|Talk on the walk does not raise falls or let tiredness pass unnoticed.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-04 Safety; bounded by VT-01
