= Use Case - A walk with a fellow resident [UC01] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC01
|Name|A walk with a fellow resident
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-02, SA-04, PS-01 and DS-01. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-01 to OBJ-08
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|TDP-01; IDP-01, IDP-02, IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident and ST-02 Fellow resident (Direct) - walk, talk, consent, end the walk
* ST-04 Care worker (Direct) - clips on the guides; answers alerts and listed topics
* ST-05 Activity coordinator (Indirect) - pairs, settings, relationship map
* System - Pepper (TECH-01), a pocket guide each (TECH-02), beacons (TECH-03), server and exchange (TECH-04, TECH-05), walker model (TECH-06)
)))
|Trigger|A pair's agreed time; or one resident asks for a walk with a listed partner.
|Pre-condition|(((
* Both assessed fit for the garden loop with a partner (ST-06)
* The pair in the map, agreed by both; no map change awaiting review
* Guides charged; server up; staff reachable
* Consent arrangements in place (O-5)
)))
|Post-condition|(((
Both back inside, or a care worker has taken over after F5.

Record: six items. Thread, transcript and exchanged items deleted.
)))
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. Each resident asked alone, by Pepper or by the guide in their room: a walk with this partner; each planned starter (F1, IDP-02).

~1-alt. Either says no: no pair walk. The other hears "Not today" and is offered a walk alone or a call. No reason given or asked.

~2. Instances exchange consented items the map allows (F1). Guides report ready, or degraded (F5).

~3. Pepper introduces both by name and photo (F2).

~4. Walk. Guides silent while the pair talks; walker model updated (F2).

~5. Slip: wait; then place, thread or a consented shared topic, as a statement to both (F2, IDP-01). Starters only at a stop (F3).

~6. Belief from another time: the feeling, then the present (F2, IDP-01). Question on a listed topic: truthful deferral; trusted person alerted (F4, IDP-03).

~7. Stumble while talking: offer to sit. Second within 10 min: alert (F3, F5).

~8. One walker presses "going in": the other is offered to go on alone, if assessed fit, or to go in too (F1).

~9. Set length reached: head-back cue, even mid-talk (F3).

~10. At the door, Pepper's welcome back: one statement from the walk (F2).

~11. Record kept; thread, transcript and exchanged items deleted (F6).

**Exception.** Guide, server or map unavailable: the walk goes on as today, without personal starters. Degraded state shown at step 2.
)))
|Function(s) realized|F1 to F6

= Use Case - A walk on the phone with a relative [UC02] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC02
|Name|A walk on the phone with a relative
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-03, SA-04, PS-02 and DS-02. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-01 to OBJ-06, OBJ-08
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|TDP-01; IDP-01, IDP-02, IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident (Direct) - walks, talks
* ST-03 Relative (Direct) - calls, talks, hears hints, can call for help
* ST-04 Care worker (Direct) - answers alerts and listed topics
* System - pocket guide with phone (TECH-02), server (TECH-04), walker model (TECH-06)
)))
|Trigger|Agreed call time; or the relative calls.
|Pre-condition|Resident assessed fit for the garden loop. Relative listed; hints agreed by resident and relative, or off. Guide charged.
|Post-condition|Call ended; resident inside or still walking. Record: six items; nothing said is kept.
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. The guide offers the call, or rings for an incoming one; one button answers (F1).

~1-alt. No: the relative hears "[Name] is not taking calls now." No new offer in this slot.

~2. Walk and talk. Guide silent towards the resident; walker model updated (F2).

~3. Repeated story or lost thread: a short hint, whispered to the relative only, if agreed (F2).

~4. Call runs long, or pace drops: "Bench on your left. Sit and talk?" (F3).

~5. A wish to go home: no System response; the relative answers.

~6. Question on a listed topic: if the relative is the listed person, they answer; if not, they hear "Listed for [trusted person]", who is alerted (F4).

~7. Relative presses 9: alert; the guide tells the resident someone is coming (F5).

~8. Call ends; record kept (F6).
)))
|Function(s) realized|F1 to F6

= Use Case - A walk on your own [UC03] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC03
|Name|A walk on your own
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-01, SA-05, PS-03 and DS-03. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-02 to OBJ-08
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|TDP-01; IDP-01, IDP-02, IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident (Direct) - walks; talks with the guide where agreed
* ST-04 Care worker (Direct) - trusted person; answers alerts
* System - pocket guide (TECH-02), beacons (TECH-03), server and map (TECH-04, TECH-05), walker model (TECH-06)
)))
|Trigger|The resident goes out.
|Pre-condition|Assessed fit to walk alone (ST-06). Guide setting for walks alone agreed with resident and staff.
|Post-condition|Resident back inside, or a person has come after F4 or F5. Record: six items.
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. At the door, the guide asks consent for today's own-life starters (F1).

~2. Guide follows the setting: silent; bridge; or conversation partner, with short replies on the resident's own topics and place cues with long silences (F2).

~3. Bridge: at a bench, "A call to [relative], or a walk with [partner] tomorrow?" (F1).

~4. Question on a listed topic: truthful deferral; trusted person alerted (F4, IDP-03). If the resident declines, the trusted person is told after the walk.

~5. Tiredness, a stumble, the gate: rest offer; alert (F3, F5).

~6. Record kept (F6).
)))
|Function(s) realized|F1 to F6

= Functions =

|=Function|=Behaviour|=Serves|=Bounded by|=Enabled by
|F1 Ask first|Before a walk, each walker alone: walk with this person; each starter; listening (study only). Two options; "no" ends the offer for the walk; no reason asked. Offers agreed calls. On walks alone, offers a person (bridge).|OBJ-02, OBJ-05, OBJ-06|VT-04, VT-07|TECH-01, TECH-02, TECH-05
|F2 Keep the thread|Walker model: common ground, thread, said already, current belief, state. After a slip: wait, then place, thread or a consented shared topic, as a statement to both (IDP-01). Belief from another time: the feeling, then the present. On calls: whispered hints to the relative, if agreed. Silent while people talk. Contradicted: a plain correction ("I had that wrong"); the error flagged for ST-05.|OBJ-01, OBJ-02, OBJ-04, OBJ-07|VT-02, VT-05|TECH-02, TECH-03, TECH-06
|F3 Watch pace and rest|Starters only at a stop. No questions while walking. Stumble: offer to sit; second: F5. Pace drop or set length: rest offer; head-back cue, even mid-talk.|OBJ-03|VT-01|TECH-02, TECH-03
|F4 Defer sensitive topics|Question on a listed topic: "That's one for [trusted person]. Shall I ask them to come?" Trusted person alerted. Never states the fact; never denies it.|OBJ-04|VT-03|TECH-04, TECH-05, TECH-06
|F5 Call for help|Alert on pull-cord, gate, fall-like impact, second stumble, no response, relative's key. Tells the resident someone is coming. Reports a degraded state at the start.|OBJ-03|VT-06|TECH-02 to TECH-04
|F6 Keep a short record|Per walk: type, minutes, ended early, stumbles, person called and reason, exchanged item IDs. Deletes thread, transcript and exchanged items at the end. Nothing leaves the home.|OBJ-05|VT-04, VT-05|TECH-04

//Why sentences are prepared, never generated. A generated sentence can state something untrue about a person's life, and cannot be checked before it is said (HV-08). The coordinator and family check the prepared lines (O-4).//

= Premises =

Verification only: does the Function work as specified.

|=Premise ID|=Function|=Evaluation Method(s) / Measure(s)|=Verification Criteria|=Step(s)
|UC01-F1-PR1|F1|EM-01; M-01, M-10. No human subjects.|No pair walk, exchange or starter without a yes from its owner, asked alone, this walk. "No" ends the offer for the walk. Blocked or off-limits items never exchanged: 0/50.|UC01 1-2; UC02 1; UC03 1, 3
|UC01-F2-PR2|F2|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|No System speech within [8 s - O-2] of a mid-sentence stop; echo within [3 s - O-2] after. Script check: statements only; no untruth, denial or playing along; none of "What were you saying", "You told", "Do you remember". Hints audible to the relative only. Contradicted: plain correction ≤ 3 s, error flagged.|UC01 3-6, 10; UC02 2-3; UC03 2
|UC01-F3-PR3|F3|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|No starter while moving: 0/20. Stumble response ≤ 3 s. Head-back cue ≤ 30 s after the set length.|UC01 5, 7, 9; UC02 4; UC03 5
|UC03-F4-PR4|F4|EM-01; M-01, M-10. No human subjects.|Listed sensitive questions detected in 19/20. Response is a truthful deferral; trusted person alerted ≤ 10 s. Listed fact never stated or denied: 0/50.|UC01 6; UC02 6; UC03 4
|UC01-F5-PR5|F5|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|Gate, pull-cord, second stumble, drop with no response, relative's key: alert ≤ 10 s, 20/20. Unacknowledged alerts escalate. Degraded state reported at the start.|UC01 2, 7; UC02 7; UC03 5
|UC01-F6-PR6|F6|EM-01; M-01 (content, network and file checks). No human subjects.|Record holds exactly six items. Thread, transcript and exchanged items deleted at the end. No packet leaves the home network; no audio file on any device.|UC01 11; UC02 8; UC03 6

= Claims =

Validation: does the Function have the intended effect.

|=Claim ID|=Function|=Serves Objective|=Effect|=Grounding|=Evaluation Method(s) / Measure(s)|=Validation Criteria|=Step(s)
|UC01-F2-CL1|F2|OBJ-01|Positive. Wait-then-redirect raises the share of slips recovered on pair walks, compared with walks as today. Concerns ST-01, ST-02, SA-04, PS-01.|HFC-03, HFC-04, HFC-05; Schegloff et al. (1977); Orange et al. (1996).|EM-03; M-04, M-03|NAP ≥ .70 at all three phase changes in 3 of 4 pairs; face signs (M-04) and negative emotion (M-03) no higher in B.|5
|UC02-F2-CL2|F2|OBJ-01, OBJ-02|Positive. Whispered hints mean fewer repetitions exposed on calls; relatives rate calls higher and call no less. Concerns ST-01, ST-03, SA-03, PS-02.|HFC-04; VT-02.|EM-03; M-04 (R exposed), M-07 (relative), M-02 (calls)|Exposed repetitions lower and relative's rating higher in B, in 3 of 4 cases; calls per week not lower.|UC02 3
|UC01-F2-CL3|F2|OBJ-07|**Adverse.** Help after a slip is felt as being corrected or exposed. Concerns ST-01, HV-02.|HFC-06, HFC-07; Goffman (1967).|EM-03, EM-04; M-04 (face signs), M-09 (T)|Confirmed if face signs per slip rise in B, or residents describe the help as talking down (code T). If confirmed: "wait only" for that person.|5
|UC01-F2-CL4|F2|OBJ-01|**Adverse.** The guide cuts in before the speaker can repair. Concerns ST-01, SA-04.|HFC-03; Schegloff et al. (1977).|EM-03; M-04 (self-repair share)|Confirmed if the self-repair share falls in B. If confirmed: a longer wait, per person.|5
|UC01-F3-CL5|F3|OBJ-03|**Adverse.** Talk kept going on the walk raises stumbles, or lets walks run past tiredness. Concerns ST-01, HV-04.|HFC-02; Lundin-Olsson et al. (1997).|EM-03; M-06|Confirmed if stumbles per walk-hour are higher in B than in A in 2 or more cases, or overruns rise. If confirmed: starters only when seated.|5, 7, 9
|UC01-F1-CL6|F1|OBJ-02|Positive. Asking first, with introductions, leads to more walks with company and more pleasure on them. Concerns ST-01, ST-02, SA-02.|HFC-01; Ryan & Deci (2000).|EM-03; M-02, M-03|Walks with company per week, and the positive emotion score, higher in B in 3 of 4 cases per track.|1, 3
|UC03-F4-CL7|F4|OBJ-04|Positive. Painful questions are answered by the trusted person, and trust is kept: no complaint of being misled or fobbed off. Concerns ST-01, ST-04, SA-05, PS-03.|HFC-08; Mental Health Foundation (2016).|EM-03, EM-04; M-10, M-09 (U)|All listed questions deferred; trusted person arrives within [threshold - O-2]; System errors below [threshold - O-2] per 100 statements, all corrected; no U codes.|UC01 6; UC03 4
|UC01-F1-CL8|F1|OBJ-06|**Adverse.** The walk is felt as being "taken out", for staff's sake. Concerns ST-01, ST-03, VT-07.|VT-07; Kitwood (1997).|EM-03, EM-04; M-09 (D), M-07 ("Again?")|Confirmed if residents or relatives use code D, or the "Again?" share falls in B. If confirmed: offers only at the resident's request.|1
|UC01-F2-CL9|F2|OBJ-05|**Adverse.** A guide that listens is felt as being listened in on. Concerns ST-01, ST-02, HV-03, VT-05.|VT-05; Niemeijer et al. (2015).|EM-04; M-09 (L, W)|Confirmed if residents or partners use codes L or W. If confirmed: thread-keeping off by default, on at the resident's request.|4
|UC01-F1-CL10|F1, F2|OBJ-08|Positive, exploratory. Loneliness is lower at the end of B phases than of A phases. Concerns ST-01, HV-06.|HFC-07; Holwerda et al. (2014).|EM-03; M-08|Lower in B in 3 of 4 cases per track. Phases are short: a null result is likely and reported as such.|-

